<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady, oil down, meal firm.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady, oil down, meal firm.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in market and plant delivery condition, dealers said on Wednesday. Arrivals in central Indian markets were limited due to the rains.</p>
<p>The undertone was steady and business volume was low.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were down on increased selling against very limited demand. Soyoil solvent was down by 300 rupees and soyoil refined was down by 400 rupees per tonne. The undertone was also easy and business volume was at the lowest level.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm on good export demand. Business volume was good and the undertone was strong. Soymeal yellow was $258-260 per tonne in export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $118-119 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,050 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,000-4,025 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
